# Define the image
# Here, replace "/home/stud/wxie/BLINK_Dataset/Counting/val/images/val_Counting_45_image_1.jpg" with the actual image file path.
# To get the bounding box coordinates of bounding boxes, you can use the function `Object_Detector_Tool.execute()`.
# However, for this example, we are simply counting the number of motors.
# The motor count is determined by counting the number of occurrences of the bounding box with coordinates:
# (for example, if the motor has bounding box coordinates (0.25, 0.5, 0.3, 0.65)) on the image:
first_motor_coords = (0.25, 0.5, 0.3, 0.65)
motor_count = sum(1 for coords in bounding_box_coords for x, y in zip(first_motor_coords[0], first_motor_coords[1]) if coords[0] <= x <= coords[2] and coords[1] <= y <= coords[3])

# Print the final result
final_result = (motor_count,)

final_result

